Suppose you have a document that requires a LaTeX documentstyle option
foobar.sty that is not part of the standard LaTeX distribution but is
a very common option file, widely available on all the standard
archives. If you send your document to a colleague, you may wish to
assume that your colleague already has a copy of foobar.sty, so that
you can save the trouble of sending him/her a copy of your copy.  Then
how do you guard against the possibility that s/he may get subtly
wrong results---no error messages---because of having version 1.2
instead of version 2.1 of foobar.sty?

